WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.350
Northern Alberta, Canada.

2
00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:09.590
Under 142,200 square kilometres of land
lies sand mixed with thick bitumen.

3
00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:14.510
Across the United States, gas is
freed from tight shale by fracking:

4
00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:17.770
water, sand and chemicals crack the rock.

5
00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:24.030
Off Brazil, oil found in 2006 lies more
than 7,000 metres below the sea surface,

6
00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:26.390
under a layer of salt.

7
00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:27.670
Sticky sand.

8
00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:28.510
Cracked rock.

9
00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:31.330
Oil beneath the deep seabed.

10
00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:33.530
Is any of it worth the cost?

11
00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:36.650
In this mission, you'll weigh
the benefits of each fuel,

12
00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:39.130
from royalties to energy security.

13
00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:44.030
Then you'll count the costs, from
carbon and land to tremors and spills,

14
00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:46.070
and ask who pays them.

15
00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:50.990
Your mission: decide whether unconventional
oil and gas are worth the cost.
